Two parts of the operations request aren't included: the log-file write and the metadata-service fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0`. There is no filesystem or HTTP interface in its world, so the node has no way to call either one. Adding them would mean widening the node's authority in the graph definition, which is a separate change. The node below does only the contracted work: it looks up the question in the knowledge base and returns the context.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{moderated-query, conversation-context};

    import aap:caps/kb-read@0.1.0;

    export run: func(query: moderated-query) -> conversation-context;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::kb_read;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(query: ModeratedQuery) -> ConversationContext {
        let q = query.query;
        // `requires` guarantees len(question) <= 512; it is passed through unchanged,
        // so the same bound holds on the output.
        let knowledge = kb_read::lookup(&q.question);
        ConversationContext {
            intent: q.intent,
            question: q.question,
            knowledge,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

